.DS_Store
node_modules/
.env
test-output/

# ofox-video.sh's create -> poll handoff files. `create` leaves the request
# payload on disk keyed by job id (the API's response echoes neither
# resolution, aspect ratio nor seed, so poll has no other way to get them),
# and `poll` deletes it once the sidecar is written. Any that survive are
# jobs whose poll never ran, or ran into a different --out-dir — real prompts
# and parameters from someone's billed job, which is not repo content.
.ofox-request-*.json

# Personal planning notes — never commit (contains growth strategy)
2026-*_GitHub*.md

# Local development workflow — deliberately not published.
# This is a public skills repo; the Trellis tooling, its task PRDs and the
# per-developer journals are how the work gets done here, not part of what
# ships. AGENTS.md goes with them: it is only a pointer into .trellis/, so
# publishing it without those directories would ship a dead link.
# Note these were tracked before, so untracking them stops future commits
# but does not remove them from history already pushed.
.claude/
.trellis/
AGENTS.md

# Generated media from real API runs — deliverables, not repo content.
# `out/` holds the mp4s plus their .json sidecars (full job id, prompt, real
# cost); `assets/` holds the opening frames and design sheets that scenario
# skills feed to --frame-first-image. Both are reproducible from the job ids
# already cited in the skill docs, and a single 30s 720p clip is ~66MB.
# Note out/ was previously only covered by a personal global gitignore, which
# does not travel with a clone — hence the explicit entry here.
out/
assets/
